{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>And He fed him</b> — All the commentators say that ויאכילהו refers to the Name mentioned above, and the heh and vav of אל ישראל — if in His ways they walk. The meaning would be: it was fitting that they listen to Him, and remember the kindness He did for their fathers, namely the eating of the manna, which is sweeter and more esteemed than the fat of wheat, and He satisfied them with water from a rock, sweeter than honey. And the mem of מצור serves as a construct, in the manner of: מאל אביך ויעזרך." "<b>And the meaning of אשביעך</b> — In the manner of: מטרף בני עלית, every seer of him says to him. Thus sometimes He speaks as though not to the face, and sometimes He speaks to the face, and likewise שמנת עבית כשית, for such is the way of the language." "And some say that ומצור דבש אשביעך — He will speak to the face of Israel in the future."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 81, :notes {0 "The phrase 'והה״א והוי״ו שב אל ישראל' literally means 'the heh and vav that are in El Yisrael'; I read it as pointing to the pronominal suffix elements in אליהם/אלהיו type forms, though the syntactic point is compressed and not fully spelled out.", 1 "Ibn Ezra cites Genesis 31:14 and 1 Samuel 21:7 (or similar locutions) as grammatical parallels; the compressed phrase 'כל רואו אומר לו' is hyper-literally 'everyone who sees him says to him,' the reference of which is obscure and possibly corrupt."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:35:52.713136504Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}